<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balša I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1362">1362</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balša I was a nobleman of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeta-region">Zeta</a> and founder of the Balšić family. After the death of the Serbian emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a> in 1355 he and his sons Stracimir, Đurađ I and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balsa-ii">Balša II</a> took control of much of Zeta, the land around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-skadar">Lake Skadar</a> in present-day Montenegro and northern Albania. He died around 1362, and his sons expanded the family's power.</p></div>
